<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Capussa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 206 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Capussa was a king of the Massylii, a Numidian people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, in the late third century BCE. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oezalces">Oezalces</a>, who had succeeded his brother Gaia, he took the throne on his father's death but was soon killed in a civil war by the noble Mazaetullus, who set up Capussa's brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lacumazes">Lacumazes</a> as king. These conflicts allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syphax">Syphax</a> to seize Massylian lands before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masinissa">Masinissa</a> returned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/capussa.jpg" alt="Capussa" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sneakier · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Capussa,_king_of_the_Massylii.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
